  "caveats": {
    "global": [
      "Web search for this build was served by the built-in Node metasearch, not SearXNG. built-in metasearch: bing(10) — unavailable: duckduckgo (bot challenge served (HTTP 202) and the proxy route could not get past it either (All 3 scraping routes failed for html.duckduckgo.com. direct: html.duckduckgo.co) — this engine has blocked us). No Docker or Python required, but materially weaker than SearXNG: Intermittent. DuckDuckGo serves a CAPTCHA after roughly 10-15 queries; Bing degrades to unrelated results once it flags the host. Both are detected and discarded rather than stored, so counts are a floor and a thin result set may mean throttling rather than competitor silence. It cannot serve the linkedin, x, event channels at all, because neither engine honours the site: operator or qualifier terms.",
      "GDELT rate-limited 4 request(s) on the last run (it allows 1 req/5s). News coverage from that source is incomplete for this build."
    ],
    "by_range": {
      "7": [],
      "30": [],
      "90": [
        "GDELT is at the edge of its ~90-day window here; some older news may be missing."
      ],
      "365": [
        "GDELT news indexing covers only a ~90-day rolling window, so 365-day web/news counts are thinner than reality."
      ]
    },
